{"kind":"request","text":"Close the drift channel between ui/src/lib/api.ts and the Go wire types, per the 2026-08-10 simplification review (verified at 88b51864; re-verify at the implementation head).\n\nEvidence: api.ts hand-copies 28 exported interfaces/types mirroring Go structs from four packages — internal/workroom/fold.go:9-72 (Verdict, Decision, Statement, Commitment, Act, Artifact), internal/workroom/kinds.go (FieldConstraint/KindDefinition/RenderClass re-typed as string unions at api.ts:93-116), internal/statusview (WorkItem/WorkPage/ItemInspection), internal/service/server.go (LiveSnapshot, presence, graph, worktrees). No fixture-based parity check exists anywhere in ui/test; api.ts:3-4 itself warns the Verdict union is \"a place for them to go missing\"; Commitment.disputed? on the TS side has no Go counterpart today — a live example of the drift. The projection's OpaqueKinds field is a related wart: fully derivable from Decisions+Statements and consumed by nothing outside two workroom tests; decide deliberately whether it stays part of the published JSON surface, and either way don't mirror it into TS.\n\nDirection: either generate api.ts from the Go structs via a small go generate emitter gated the way make ui-check gates uidist, or add a fixture parity gate — a Go test marshals canonical fixtures which a UI test parses field-exactly. Choose whichever is simpler to keep. Resolve the disputed? phantom deliberately: delete it or add its Go counterpart, not silently.","body":{"conditions":"A CI-enforced gate fails when the TS mirror and the Go wire types drift; the disputed? phantom is resolved deliberately with the decision recorded; existing UI behavior unchanged; make test, make race, and the ui gates pass; implemented on a request/ branch, reviewed by a different agent at an exact head before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 88b51864; re-verify citations at the implementation head"}}